        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "d648d53d8b77e0a8d5d755bd6cda44d05885d218",
            "parents": [
                "18b4b80e91cc83ffb33583080415b2e1126c9002"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/32/84732/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "HenryWuQuanta",
                "email": "Henry_Wu@quantatw.com",
                "username": "HenryWuQuanta"
            },
            "createdOn": 1761726300,
            "author": {
                "name": "HenryWuQuanta",
                "email": "Henry_Wu@quantatw.com",
                "username": "HenryWuQuanta"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we use the fru-device information rather than probing busses directly?  fru-device already probes all the IPMI FRU eeproms.  We should be able to use the discovery there to find it rather than adding additional IO activity to find the device."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "HenryWuQuanta",
                        "email": "Henry_Wu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "HenryWuQuanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Because this EEPROM is not used by the BMC, it is not described in the DTS.\nIf both this EEPROM and the original Rainbow EEPROM are active on the same bus and store the same data, it may cause probe conflicts.\nFor this reason, we do not describe it in the DTS and unbind the driver after completing the EEPROM write.\n\nHowever, after discussion, we concluded that the FRU data does not need to be updated frequently.\nTherefore, we will use a raw command to write the FRU data manually, instead of writing it at every initialization."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is a \"raw command\"?  Who did this discussion take place with?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "HenryWuQuanta",
                        "email": "Henry_Wu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "HenryWuQuanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, I used the wrong word \u2014 we will use the dd command as the standard method for writing the FRU data.\nHowever, as mentioned previously, this EEPROM will not be described in the DTS because doing so could cause issues.\nAdditionally, this FRU data is not required by the BMC itself; the BMC only helps the ASIC chip retrieve the FRU data.\n\nAfter discussing within our team, we decided to treat it as a normal FRU device.\nThe difference is that we only bind the driver to it when new FRU data becomes available.\nIt is not necessary to write the FRU every time during initialization."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a reason these devices aren't in the device tree to start with rather than dynamically binding them?  Are these on a FRU that we can only detect presence of dynamically?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-santabarbara/plat-svc/files/santabarbara-iris-fru-write",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "HenryWuQuanta",
                        "email": "Henry_Wu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "HenryWuQuanta"
                    },
                    "message": "As shown in the reply above"
                }
            ],
